INSTALLATION
	First of all you need yo compile the XSTEP-3.5.1 library.
INSTALLING XSTEP
	Download it at http://xstep.sourceforge.net/ and extract it:

		 tar -zxvf xstep-3.5.1.tar.gz

	To compile the XSTEP library,cd to the library dir

		cd xstep-3.5.1
		cd library

	and just type:

		make

	Your system must be a unix-like system and must have the X headers
	and libraries (X11R6 is recommended), any 32 bit C compiler w/
	support for shared libraries (GCC is recomended) and any 'make'
	(GNU and BSD makes are recommended).

	If you don't receive any error message, a shared library will be
	generated in the directory 'library'. You can install this library
	(and XSTEP headers) typing:

		make install

	You can uninstall XSTEP any time with:

		make uninstall

INSTALLING XSTEPFILEMANAGER
	Download it and extract it:

	tar -zxvf xstepfilemanager-xxb.tar.gz

	To compile xstepfilemanager, cd to the xstepfilemanager dir 
	and take a look at the Config.h file where you can configure
	the behaviour of xstepfilemanager:
	
	#define LABEL    "XstepFileManager 0.6beta"
	
	/* Here you can define your preferred helper apps */

	#define TERMINAL "aterm"
	#define TERM_EXE "aterm -e"
	#define EDITOR   "aterm -e e3"
	/*#define VIEWER   "aterm -e less"*/

	/* to enable internal viewer */
	#define INTERNAL_VIEWER
		#ifdef INTERNAL_VIEWER
		#undef VIEWER
		#endif
	
	/* to enable right-click menus */
	/*#define RIGHT_CLICK */
	
	/* for debugging */
	/*#define DEBUG*/

	then just type:

		make

	If you don't receive any error message, you can install xstepfilemanager typing:

		make install

	You can uninstall xstepfilemanager any time with:

		make uninstall
	
	You can run xstepfilemanager by double-clicking it or from
	a shell with:

	./xstepfilemanager 

	or

	xstepfilemanager (if it is in your path variable).
	
	You can run xstepfilemanager applet xrun by double-clicking it or from a shell.
	You can run xstepfilemanager applet xviewer only from a shell as it needs a 
	filename as argument:
	
	./xviewer foo.txt
	
	or

	xviewer foo.txt

USAGE
	The GUI is self explanatory (.... I hope).

